## Propagating Trace Context Across RabbitMQ

The issue is that RabbitMQ doesn't automatically carry W3C `traceparent`/`tracestate` headers. You need to **inject** context into message headers on publish and **extract** it on consume.

### Service A — Publisher (Inject)

```csharp
using System.Diagnostics;
using OpenTelemetry;
using OpenTelemetry.Context.Propagation;
using RabbitMQ.Client;

private static readonly ActivitySource Source = new("ServiceA");
private static readonly TextMapPropagator Propagator = Propagators.DefaultTextMapPropagator;

public void PublishOrder(Order order, IModel channel)
{
    using var activity = Source.StartActivity("OrderPublished", ActivityKind.Producer);

    var props = channel.CreateBasicProperties();
    props.Headers ??= new Dictionary<string, object>();

    // Inject current trace context into message headers
    Propagator.Inject(
        new PropagationContext(activity!.Context, Baggage.Current),
        props.Headers,
        (headers, key, value) => headers[key] = value);

    var body = JsonSerializer.SerializeToUtf8Bytes(order);
    channel.BasicPublish("orders-exchange", "order.created", props, body);
}
```

### Service B — Consumer (Extract)

```csharp
using System.Diagnostics;
using System.Text;
using OpenTelemetry;
using OpenTelemetry.Context.Propagation;

private static readonly ActivitySource Source = new("ServiceB");
private static readonly TextMapPropagator Propagator = Propagators.DefaultTextMapPropagator;

public void HandleMessage(BasicDeliverEventArgs ea)
{
    // Extract trace context from incoming message headers
    var parentContext = Propagator.Extract(
        default,
        ea.BasicProperties.Headers,
        (headers, key) =>
        {
            if (headers.TryGetValue(key, out var val))
            {
                // RabbitMQ stores header values as byte[]
                return new[] { val is byte[] bytes ? Encoding.UTF8.GetString(bytes) : val.ToString()! };
            }
            return Enumerable.Empty<string>();
        });

    Baggage.Current = parentContext.Baggage;

    // This activity becomes a child of Service A's producer span
    using var activity = Source.StartActivity(
        "OrderReceived",
        ActivityKind.Consumer,
        parentContext.ActivityContext);

    var order = JsonSerializer.Deserialize<Order>(ea.Body.Span);
    ProcessOrder(order!);
}
```

### OpenTelemetry Setup (both services)

```csharp
builder.Services.AddOpenTelemetry()
    .WithTracing(tracing => tracing
        .AddSource("ServiceA") // or "ServiceB"
        .AddAspNetCoreInstrumentation()
        .AddOtlpExporter());
```

### Key points

- **`Propagators.DefaultTextMapPropagator`** handles W3C TraceContext + Baggage by default.
- RabbitMQ stores header values as `byte[]`, so the extract callback must decode them.
- The consumer passes `parentContext.ActivityContext` as the **parent** when starting its activity — this links both spans into one trace.
- If you use MassTransit or NServiceBus, this is done automatically; raw `RabbitMQ.Client` requires manual propagation as shown above.
